<section>

<div class="faq-box">

<h1 class="section-title">Entry to multiple attractions with Aquarium World</h1>

<p id="introduction">Home to over 1000 species across 10 themed zones, there's so much to explore at Aquarium World:</p>

<ul>

<li> Adventure - Journey through icy Arctic and Antarctic landscapes and get up close with our colony of Gentoo Penguins</li>
<li>Ocean Invaders - Step into an immersive jellyfish experience spanning several unique underwater environments</li>
<li>Coral Kingdom - Dive into a breathtaking underwater world and discover our thriving living coral reef</li>
<li>Rockpool Discovery - Uncover what lies beneath the surface of local seas and meet the creatures found closer to home.</li>

</ul>

</div>

</section>

<div class="everything">
<h1>Marine Zones Details</h1>
</div>

<section class="zone-drawers">

<div class="firstblock">

<details class="drawer">
  <summary>Aquarium World</summary>
<p>Aquarium World is organized into several themed marine zones, each offering visitors a chance to explore different aquatic environments and their inhabitants.</p>
</details>

<details class="drawer">
  <summary>Coral Reef Zone</summary>
  <p>Coral Reef Zone invites guests into a vibrant underwater world built around a living coral reef. Visitors can spot the bright yellow tang, a reef fish known for grazing on algae, alongside clownfish, which live safely among sea anemones thanks to their natural immunity to the anemones' sting. The exhibit also highlights how coral reefs themselves are formed by tiny animals called polyps, and how they support thousands of marine species.</p>
</details>

<details class="drawer">
  <summary>Deep Sea Trench</summary>
  <p>Deep Sea Trench takes visitors on a descent into darker ocean depths, home to jellyfish, creatures that have drifted through the seas for over 500 million years, as well as sharks, including the calm, distinctively spotted leopard shark. This zone emphasizes the ancient origins and ecological importance of these predators.</p>
</details>

</div>

<div class="Secondblock">
<details class="drawer">
  <summary>Coastal Rockpools</summary>
  <p>Coastal Rockpools offers a hands-on, supervised area where guests can get close to smaller shoreline creatures: crabs, shrimp, sea snails, and hermit crabs, which famously borrow empty shells to live in as they grow. It's a more intimate, local counterpart to the deeper zones.</p>
</details>

<details class="drawer">
  <summary>Freshwater Rivers &amp; Rainforest</summary>
  <p>Freshwater Rivers &amp; Rainforest follows the journey of water from rivers to the sea, introducing long-living sea turtles that return to their birth beaches to nest, and highly intelligent dolphins that rely on echolocation to navigate and hunt.</p>
</details>

<details class="drawer">
  <summary>Character Cove</summary>
  <p>Character Cove, the family-friendly zone, uses more playful, cartoon-style presentations to introduce younger visitors to eels, sea snakes, stingrays, and octopuses, the latter notable for having three hearts and remarkable intelligence among invertebrates.</p>
</details>

</div>

</section>

